    "body": "Blocked. No code written and no branch pushed.\n\nWhy this can't be done safely yet:\n\n1. **Rotary feed depends on held PR #951 (#885).** A simultaneous XYZA feed has to hold the microARC 4's stated A rate. #951 adds the shared rule that does this (`crates/post/src/post/rotary_cap.rs`: `rotaryRate` / `rotaryFeedCap` / `rotaryFeed`). Its body says `tormach.cps` needs no cap only because it refuses an A that changes inside an operation. #951 is unmerged (needs-rework), and #952 is stacked on it. A second copy of that rule in `tormach.cps` would duplicate it and conflict with it. Posting wrapped A with no rate cap would let F carry A past its rate, and that output is not safe.\n2. **The two open questions on this issue are still unanswered.** One is whether PathPilot wraps A (rollover) or treats it as linear degrees. The other is how it reads F on a combined XYZA move (G94 or G93). The public LinuxCNC docs leave rollover to each machine's configuration (the wrapped-rotary joint setting), and the Tormach guides don't say which one the microARC 4 uses. The issue's own Work list says to settle both in the PathPilot Hub and on the 770MX first, and \"Done means\" includes a cut on the hardware. An agent can do neither.\n\nUntil then, the safe state on main stays as it is: `tormach.cps` refuses by name an A that changes inside an operation (\"simultaneous 4-axis motion ... not confirmed on PathPilot\"), and `microarc_test_part::a_wrapped_op_on_the_test_part_is_refused_by_name` pins that.\n\nUnblocks when: #951 merges (so the shared rate rule exists), and the rollover and feed-mode answers are recorded here from a Hub run or the machine.\n",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
    "pin": null,
