    "body": "Status update (M5, 2026-11-17):\n\n- **Blocker 1 is solved.** The shared rotary-feed cap from #885 shipped in v0.19.0 (PR #951 moved to #1395 in this repository). A simultaneous XYZA feed can now hold the microARC 4's stated A rate.\n- **Blocker 2 stays: two PathPilot answers.** A Hub kit is ready for mkinney to run on the 770MX sim with the A axis on (`hub-tests/796-microarc-a-axis/`, four tiny programs that move only X and A):\n  1. A rollover: from A350, does `G1 A10` turn +20 deg (wrap) or -340 deg? And what does the A DRO read afterwards?\n  2. Feed on a combined X+A move in G94 (`G1 X4 A180 F20`): about 12 s means F counts the X length only; minutes means the A degrees count as length too.\n  3. The same move in G93 (`F5` = 12 s), or the exact refusal.\n  4. A pure A move in G94 (`G1 A180 F360`): about 30 s if F is degrees per minute.\n\nThe readings will be recorded here. With them, the continuous wrapped-A posting can be specified, and #1904's continuous 4-axis walkthrough can follow.\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
