    "body": "**Hub reading 1 (A rollover), 2026-11-17 00:39 PST, PathPilot v2.14.4, 770MX SIM, 4th axis on (4\" 4th Axis type), run by mkinney, read by M5 from the screen recording:**\n\nFrom `G0 A350`, the move `G1 A10 F360` turned A **backwards through 340 deg**: the A DRO read 350.000, 333.9, 297.7, 261.8, 229.6, 190.5, 154.6, 117.7, 81.6, 46.4, 28.8 and stopped at **10.000** (not 370). It did not take the short way forward and did not wrap at 360. The 340 deg took about 57 s, which is 360 deg/min: on a pure A move in G94, F is degrees per minute.\n\nSo PathPilot treats A as a **linear axis in degrees, with no rollover**. A continuous wrapped-A program must keep A counting (370, 380, ...) and must never rely on the control to take the short way or to wrap.\n\nStill to come: the G94 and G93 readings for a combined X+A move (tests 2 and 3).\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
