    "body": "**Hub reading 2 (feed on a combined X+A move, G94), 2026-11-17 00:44 PST, same setup, read by M5 from the screen recording:**\n\n`G1 X4 A180 F20` (G94) took about **12 s**. The DROs every 2 s: X 0.476 / A 20.6, X 1.151 / A 51.8, X 1.825 / A 82.9, X 2.482 / A 110.9, X 3.142 / A 140.5, X 3.818 / A 172.6, then X 4.000 / A 180. X ran at about 20 in/min the whole move, and A kept pace.\n\nSo in G94 PathPilot applies **F to the XYZ distance only; the rotary follows in the same time**. The A degrees are not counted as length. Consequences for the post:\n- A combined XYZA move at F gets the XYZ feed the CAM asked for; the A speed is whatever the time allows, so the post must cap F where A would exceed the microARC 4's stated rate (the #885 rule, already on main).\n- A move that is nearly all rotation (small XYZ, large A) runs as fast as its tiny XYZ distance allows: the cap matters most there. G93 (inverse time) avoids that, if PathPilot accepts it: test 3 checks that next.\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
    "pin": null,
